				<section class="surrybg py-5">
					<div class="container-sm">
						<div class="page rounded border">

							<div class="d-xl-none">
	<div class="accordion accordion-flush rounded" id="homepageTabs">

					<div class="accordion-item">
				<h2 class="accordion-header">
					<button class="accordion-button fs-3 " type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse1" aria-expanded="true " aria-controls="collapse1">
						Virginia Residents
					</button>
				</h2>
				<div id="collapse1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#homepageTabs">
					<div class="accordion-body">
						<p>Surry Community College welcomes students from Virginia to enroll in its diverse range of programs. For Virginia residents interested in <a href="https://workforce.surry.edu" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Workforce Training</a> certifications and courses, SCC offers the benefit of paying the same tuition rates as in-state students.</p><p><a class="btn-primary-surry" href="https://surry.edu/virginia-residents">Learn More</a></p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="accordion-item">
				<h2 class="accordion-header">
					<button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse2" aria-expanded=" false " aria-controls="collapse2">
						Veterans
					</button>
				</h2>
				<div id="collapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse " data-bs-parent="#homepageTabs">
					<div class="accordion-body">
						<p>Through the Veteran's Center at Surry Community College, veterans have the opportunity to take advantage of educational benefits. These benefits vary based on the chapter, and eligibility is determined by the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA).</p><p><a class="btn-primary-surry" href="https://surry.edu/paying-for-college/veteran-services">Learn More</a></p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="accordion-item">
				<h2 class="accordion-header">
					<button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse3" aria-expanded=" false " aria-controls="collapse3">
						English Learners
					</button>
				</h2>
				<div id="collapse3" class="accordion-collapse collapse " data-bs-parent="#homepageTabs">
					<div class="accordion-body">
						<p>Surry Community College offers a variety of services and classes designed to support English Learners in their educational and professional growth. Among these programs are the English Language Acquisition (ELA) classes and the Citizenship Pathway classes.</p><h3>English Language Acquisition (ELA) Classes</h3><p>The ELA program provides students the opportunity to learn English for free, accommodating all levels—from beginners to advanced. These classes focus on all areas of language acquisition, including reading, writing, and speaking. They are designed to help students adapt to American culture and develop skills for daily life in the United States. ELA students also have the option to work toward earning their High School Equivalency diploma.</p><p><a class="btn-primary-surry" href="https://surry.edu/areas-of-study/college-and-career-readiness/english-language-acquisitions">Learn More</a></p><h3>Citizenship Pathway Classes</h3><p>Surry Community College offers a <a href="https://surry.edu/areas-of-study/college-and-career-readiness/citizenship-pathway">Citizen Pathway</a> course to prepare students with the resources, guidance, and skills needed to navigate the U.S. citizenship application process. This flexible course is available on the Dobson campus Monday through Thursday from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m., and Monday through Wednesday from 5 p.m. to 8 p.m. All classes are free of charge. Contact Roberto Hoepelman, ELA Coordinator, at (336) 386-3660 or <a href="mailto:hoepelmanra@surry.edu">hoepelmanra@surry.edu</a>.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="accordion-item">
				<h2 class="accordion-header">
					<button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse4" aria-expanded=" false " aria-controls="collapse4">
						High School
					</button>
				</h2>
				<div id="collapse4" class="accordion-collapse collapse " data-bs-parent="#homepageTabs">
					<div class="accordion-body">
						<p>Surry Community College offers incoming and current high school students multiple pathways to educational success. Current high school students can earn college credit tuition-free through our Career and College Promise (CCP) dual enrollment program. Students interested in dual enrollment should contact the SCC advising office and their high school counselor.</p><p>Incoming high school students have the opportunity to earn a 2-year Associate degree at the same time as they earn their high school diploma through the <a href="https://surry.edu/apply-now/early-college">early college school</a>. Students interested in attending the early college should speak with their middle school counselor.</p><p><a class="btn-primary-surry" href="https://surry.edu/areas-of-study/high-school">Learn More</a></p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="accordion-item">
				<h2 class="accordion-header">
					<button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse5" aria-expanded=" false " aria-controls="collapse5">
						Homeschool
					</button>
				</h2>
				<div id="collapse5" class="accordion-collapse collapse " data-bs-parent="#homepageTabs">
					<div class="accordion-body">
						<h3>Earn Your Associate Degree while in High School</h3><ul><li data-list-item-id="e00371ce7c6c23bcbaf3f74fd5711e70f">Homeschool students have flexible schedules, so they often have the unique opportunity to earn their full Associate in Arts and/or Associate in Science while still in high school by dually enrolling at Surry Community College.</li><li data-list-item-id="e02dfd1456860ec32dc3af8b41af47b20">Homeschool students are allotted one year as a high school junior (fall, spring, summer), and one year as a high school senior (fall, spring, summer) in the Career &amp; College Promise (CCP) dual enrollment program.</li><li data-list-item-id="e1485a0fbf0eb9873ebdcaf4a789a1cea">Hands-on classes offered at the Public Safety Complex in Mount Airy, the Elkin Center in Elkin, and the Yadkin Center in Yadkinville. Online class options are also available.</li><li data-list-item-id="e18434c61295abd8936b69add06214ace">Homeschool students receive free tuition. Textbook/materials and fees are not included in tuition.</li></ul><p><a class="btn-primary-surry" href="https://surry.edu/areas-of-study/high-school/career-and-college-promise/homeschool">Learn More</a></p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="accordion-item">
				<h2 class="accordion-header">
					<button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse6" aria-expanded=" false " aria-controls="collapse6">
						Purpose Center
					</button>
				</h2>
				<div id="collapse6" class="accordion-collapse collapse " data-bs-parent="#homepageTabs">
					<div class="accordion-body">
						<h3>Let us Help you Find Your Purpose!</h3><p>If you're seeking direction for your future, visit the Surry Community College Purpose Center. Open to everyone, the Purpose Center offers guidance to help you discover your purpose, explore career options, and pursue a meaningful path forward.</p><p><a class="btn-primary-surry" href="https://surry.edu/purpose-center" target="_blank">Learn More</a></p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			</div>
</div>
